              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                We found lookalike sites using PEScience's name on unusual domains. Fake protein can be underdosed or contaminated, which defeats the purpose of buying it. Stick to PEScience's own site, Amazon listings sold by PEScience or Amazon, and established retailers, and check the seal and lot number on arrival.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating Select Vegan as the same product</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Select Vegan is a different formula, a pea and brown rice blend with about 20 g of protein, stevia sweetening and higher sodium. It does not taste or mix like the dairy Select, and buyer reviews are more mixed. Judge it on its own label and reviews before buying.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the casein in the blend</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Milk protein isolate is mostly casein, so Select digests more slowly and feels heavier than whey isolate. That is good for fullness and baking, but some people find it too thick after training. Use more liquid, or keep a lighter whey isolate for immediately after workouts.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming third-party tested means certified</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                PEScience says its protein is third-party tested for purity and potency, but it does not advertise NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport status. Drug-tested athletes need a product they can look up in a public certification database by exact product and flavor before they buy it.
              </p>
            </div>
